  "note": "Diagnostic source-inclusion harness recompiles unchanged production distance/mesh modules under example-local symbols. Whole and staged modes alternate in one process/pool on the same unchanged measured-source TIN. Staged mode retains original serial Morton preparation, 4096-point indexed query chunks, chunk-local previous-hit/cached stack, exact unsigned f64 arithmetic and compact serial scatter. Full distances, six statistics and scalar PLY match an independent archived production oracle on every call. Original mesh vectors move without coordinate copies/transforms/reordering. BVH construction, Morton bounds/keys/sort/index extraction, parallel query/collection including chunk scratch destruction, final allocation/serial scatter including result-chunk destruction, and explicit order/BVH destruction are measured separately. Remaining pool-installation/timer/dispatch costs are unattributed. Loading, TIN/pool construction, first use, five warmups, serialization/statistics/parity and cleanup are excluded. Ten alternating pairs and all outliers are retained. Stage timers, source-included symbol/code layout, closure state and compilation can change timing; output parity establishes correctness, not timing equivalence to the archived binary. Diagnostic percentages are not an optimization or a production speedup claim. Shares are medians of per-trial fractions and need not sum to 100%. Production source/configuration fingerprints remain unchanged. Native-only profiling; no browser/WASM/GPU/Python conversion speedup claim. No GPU model identifiers collected. Clocks/power/scheduling/other applications/allocator/retained pages are uncontrolled. No builds/tests/scans/edits run alongside timing."
